  "identity": "Joint UT–VU Creative Technology BSc, Amsterdam, English, 2026–2027",
  "curriculum": "The 2026–2027 EEMCS Creative Technology EER, section B Article 1.2 Table 1, and the current VU curriculum establish the English-taught Amsterdam location of the joint UT–VU degree. Eight mandatory module slots total 120 EC. Humane by Design is the Amsterdam-delivered module-five choice; the other choices are available at UT. The example retains the location-representative choice independently of UCR fit. The 15 EC module includes a core (3.5 EC), Utopia and Designing Futures Project (6 EC), Fairness in Data Science (5 EC), and professional development (0.5 EC). The associated module-eight choice is Dangerous Design (2.5 EC). Year three has a 30 EC approved minor or exchange and a graduation semester with Academic Writing (5 EC), Reflection (5 EC), and two project parts (5 and 15 EC). The 12 reader components preserve coherent modules; the study-unit list records their individual weights.",
  "progression": "EER B1.8 requires 60 year-one and 30 year-two EC before minor study. Module 11 non-project study units require 60 year-one and 45 year-two EC. Graduation Project normally requires all 120 EC of modules 1–8, with limited pending-result and dispensation provisions. The second project part follows completion of the first. The EER also bars concurrent major projects across modules. The standard sequential route satisfies these conditions. The minor is genuine approved space with restrictions on internships, external courses, overlap and project participation. The final design assignment uses a public presentation and defence.",
